    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0156" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg114"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 467.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of January 16 (No. 299) has
                    been received, and I have submitted to the President the resolutions which were
                    presented to you by the executive committee of the Emancipation Society. The
                    President approves of the address which you made on that occasion, and
                    authorizes you, in any proper manner, to make known to the gentlemen of the
                    committee his high appreciation of the liberal and friendly sentiments towards
                    this country which they have expressed in their resolutions.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
